SCHULEFLOW UGANDA
Product Requirements & System Features Specification
Product: SchuleFlow – Examination, Marks Management and Student Report Generation System
Target Market: Private secondary schools in Uganda
Product Version: MVP – Version 1.0

1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
1.1 What we want to build
SchuleFlow is a web-based examination, marks management and student report-generation system designed primarily for secondary schools in Uganda.
The purpose is to simplify the process of collecting examination marks, calculating student performance, identifying errors, analyzing academic results and generating student report cards.
The system should reduce teachers' administrative workload, minimize errors during examination processing and help Directors of Studies (DOS) and school administrators make better academic decisions.
1.2 The problem we want to solve
Many schools still depend on paper-based marksheets, Excel spreadsheets and manual calculations to process examination results.
This creates several challenges:
Teachers spend too much time transferring marks.
Excel formulas can break or produce incorrect calculations.
Student marks can be entered against the wrong names.
Missing marks are sometimes discovered late.
Directors of Studies spend considerable time compiling results.
Report cards take too long to prepare.
Parents sometimes wait too long to receive student reports.
SchuleFlow should address these problems without forcing schools to abandon their existing examination processes.
1.3 Our main product promise
Enter marks once. Verify automatically. Generate accurate reports quickly.
The system should allow schools to continue setting, printing, administering and marking examinations as they currently do, while SchuleFlow handles the administrative work of processing results.

2. TARGET USERS AND SYSTEM ROLES
The system should support different users with different access permissions.
A. School Administrator
Responsible for managing the school's general information and system configuration.
Can:
Register and manage students.
Register classes and streams.
Register subjects.
Register teachers.
Assign teachers to subjects and classes.
Create examination periods.
Manage user accounts.
Configure grading systems and report templates.
View school-wide academic performance.
B. Director of Studies (DOS)
Responsible for supervising examination processing and approving results.
Can:
View marks submitted by teachers.
Monitor marks submission progress.
Identify missing marks.
Review suspicious or incorrect entries.
Return marksheets to teachers for correction.
Approve examination results.
Generate class and school performance reports.
Compare subject and class performance.
C. Teacher
Responsible for entering and submitting student marks.
Can:
View assigned classes and subjects.
View student lists.
Enter marks.
Upload existing Excel marksheets.
Review entered marks.
Identify missing marks.
Submit marks to the DOS.
Correct marksheets returned for revision.
View submission status.
D. Headteacher
Responsible for overall academic supervision.
Can:
View approved examination results.
View school performance summaries.
Compare class performance.
View subject performance.
Approve or authorize final report publication.
Access academic reports.
E. Parent/Guardian (Future Feature)
Can:
Access their child's approved reports.
View academic progress.
Download report cards.
Receive school notifications.
Parent access should be optional and introduced in a later version.

