MODULE 8: CBC ASSESSMENT AND AUTOMATIC CALCULATIONS
This is an important area of specialization for SchuleFlow.
The calculation engine should support the assessment structure used by the school.
For the initial configuration, support:
Formative assessment / Activities of Integration (Classwork): out of 3.
Summative assessment (Examination): out of 100.
Classwork contribution: 20%.
Examination contribution: 80%.
Example:
Classwork = 2.5/3
Examination = 75/100
Final score:
(2.5 ÷ 3 × 20) + (75 ÷ 100 × 80) = 76.67%
Features:
Automatic weighted calculations.
Configurable assessment components.
Configurable assessment weights.
Configurable maximum marks.
Configurable rounding rules.
Automatic grade assignment.
Configurable grading scales.
Support for multiple assessment components.
Recalculation whenever marks are corrected.
Validation that assessment weights add up correctly.
The system must not hardcode one grading or assessment structure for every school.
The calculation rules should be configurable and aligned with the applicable curriculum and school requirements.
MODULE 9: AUTOMATIC ERROR DETECTION AND VALIDATION
SchuleFlow should prevent errors before reports are generated.
The system should detect:
Marks exceeding maximum scores.
Negative marks.
Missing marks.
Duplicate entries.
Students assigned to incorrect classes.
Marks entered under the wrong subject.
Unmatched student admission numbers.
Incomplete marksheets.
Unusual changes to previously submitted marks.
The system should highlight errors and explain what needs to be corrected.
It should distinguish between genuinely missing marks, authorized exemptions and students who did not sit an examination.
The system should never silently replace or invent missing marks.
MODULE 10: RESULTS REVIEW AND APPROVAL
Introduce a structured approval workflow.
Proposed process:
Teacher enters marks.
Teacher saves and submits marks.
DOS receives submitted marksheets.
DOS reviews the results.
DOS approves or returns the marksheet for correction.
Teacher makes corrections where necessary.
DOS approves the final marks.
Authorized school leadership publishes the results.
Features:
Submission tracking.
Pending approval dashboard.
Approve and reject actions.
Comments when returning marksheets.
Resubmission after correction.
Approval timestamps.
User activity history.
Lock approved marksheets against unauthorized changes.
Any change after approval must require authorization and be recorded in an audit trail.
