MODULE 13: A-LEVEL ASSESSMENT AND AUTOMATIC CALCULATIONS (S5 AND S6)
SchuleFlow must support Advanced Level examination processing for Senior Five (S5) and Senior Six (S6).
Unlike O-Level, A-Level assessment involves principal subjects, subsidiary subjects, subject combinations, grades and points. The system should therefore have a separate A-Level calculation engine.
A. A-Level Subject Configuration
The system should allow administrators to:
Register A-Level subjects.
Identify principal subjects.
Identify subsidiary subjects.
Assign subjects to students.
Configure subject combinations.
Assign teachers to subjects.
Configure assessment components.
Configure grading scales.
Configure grade-to-point conversions.
Configure aggregation rules.
Each student should have an individual subject combination based on the subjects they are registered to study.
The system should accommodate different combinations offered by different schools.
B. A-Level Marks Entry
Teachers should be able to enter marks for S5 and S6 students using the same convenient spreadsheet-style interface used for O-Level.
Features:
Select S5 or S6.
Select subject and examination.
View registered students.
Enter individual student marks.
Import marks from Excel.
Export marksheets.
Automatically calculate totals and averages where applicable.
Identify missing marks.
Detect invalid entries.
Submit results for DOS approval.
C. A-Level Examination Calculations
The system should support:
Automatic calculation of examination totals.
Automatic conversion of marks into grades.
Automatic conversion of grades into points.
Calculation of principal subject points.
Calculation of subsidiary subject grades and points where applicable.
Calculation of student aggregates.
Comparison of student performance across subjects.
Calculation of class and subject performance summaries.
The grading scales, point conversions and aggregation rules must be configurable and based on the applicable UNEB requirements or the school's approved internal assessment policy.
D. Principal and Subsidiary Subject Management
The system must distinguish between principal and subsidiary subjects.
Features:
Identify each student's principal subjects.
Identify subsidiary subjects.
Configure the number of principal subjects used in aggregation.
Apply the correct point conversion to each subject category.
Prevent subsidiary subjects from being treated as principal subjects.
Display principal and subsidiary results separately.
The system should support different A-Level combinations without assuming that all students study the same subjects.
E. A-Level Aggregation and Performance Analysis
Provide automatic calculation of student aggregates using the school's selected and approved aggregation rules.
Features:
Calculate principal subject points.
Calculate applicable subsidiary points.
Generate the student's aggregate.
Display individual subject grades.
Display individual subject points.
Compare performance across combinations.
Generate class performance summaries.
Identify students with improving or declining performance.
The aggregation engine should be configurable to accommodate applicable UNEB examination rules and school-based examination reporting.
Do not hardcode one aggregation formula for every examination type.
F. A-Level Report Card Generation
A-Level student reports should be different from O-Level reports.
The report card should display:
Student name.
Admission number.
Class (S5 or S6).
Academic year and term.
Subject combination.
Principal subjects.
Subsidiary subjects.
Marks obtained per subject.
Grades per subject.
Points per subject where applicable.
Overall aggregate where applicable.
Teacher comments.
Class teacher comments.
Director of Studies comments.
Headteacher comments.
General academic performance remarks.
The system should generate individual and class-wide A-Level reports in PDF format.
G. A-Level Academic Progress Tracking
Allow schools to monitor student performance from S5 through S6.
Features:
Compare S5 and S6 performance.
Track performance in individual subjects.
Monitor changes in grades and points.
View previous examination results.
Identify students requiring academic support.
Maintain a continuous A-Level academic record.
H. A-Level Results and Analytics Dashboard
The DOS and school administrators should be able to:
View performance by subject.
Compare different subject combinations.
Identify the best-performing students.
Identify subjects with declining performance.
View class averages.
Monitor marks submission.
Generate A-Level examination performance summaries.
I. Important A-Level System Requirements
The developer must ensure that:
A-Level and O-Level calculations are handled separately.
Principal and subsidiary subjects are clearly distinguished.
Subject combinations can be configured.
Grading and points systems are configurable.
Different internal examination formats can be supported.
School-based examination aggregates are distinguishable from official UACE results and aggregates.
Calculation rules can be updated without rebuilding the entire system.
The system must be tested against independently verified A-Level calculation examples before deployment.

