4. SCHULEFLOW SMART MARKSHEET SCANNING (FUTURE COMPETITIVE FEATURE)
We want to eventually introduce a feature that allows teachers to photograph or scan their existing printed marksheets.
The purpose is to reduce manual data entry without changing how examinations are printed or administered.
Proposed workflow:
Teacher photographs or uploads a marksheet.
SchuleFlow detects the table structure.
OCR extracts student names, admission numbers and marks.
The system matches students against registered student records.
The system identifies uncertain or unreadable entries.
The teacher reviews extracted information.
Teacher confirms the information.
Marks are transferred into the appropriate examination records.
Important requirements:
Do not require special examination paper printing.
Do not require special barcodes on every examination paper.
Support ordinary printed marksheets where technically feasible.
Use admission numbers for reliable student matching.
Provide manual correction for poor-quality scans.
Never automatically approve uncertain extracted marks.
Keep scanning optional.
This feature should be developed after the core marks management and report generation modules are working reliably.

