Each school should have:
Its own account.
Its own users.
Its own students.
Its own examination records.
Its own report templates.
Its own configurations.
One school must never access another school's private information.
B. Security
Secure password storage.
Role-based permissions.
Secure sessions.
HTTPS.
Database backups.
Audit logs.
Protection against unauthorized access.
Validation of uploaded files.
Secure school data separation.
C. Reliability
Prevent accidental deletion of approved results.
Save marks safely.
Maintain transaction integrity.
Provide clear error messages.
Maintain a history of important changes.
Allow database backup and restoration.
D. Performance
Handle hundreds or thousands of students per school.
Support multiple teachers working simultaneously.
Allow bulk marks entry.
Generate reports efficiently.
Avoid unnecessary page loading.
E. Usability
Simple navigation.
Minimal training requirements.
Clear instructions.
Easy-to-read tables.
