Before launching, the system must successfully demonstrate the following:
An administrator can register a school and configure its classes, subjects and teachers.
An administrator can register students individually and import them from Excel.
A teacher can access only their assigned classes and subjects.
A teacher can enter and save marks.
A teacher can import an existing Excel marksheet.
The system can identify invalid and missing marks.
The calculation engine produces correct results against independently verified test cases.
The DOS can review, approve or return submitted marksheets.
Approved marks cannot be changed without authorization.
The system can generate an individual student report card.
The system can generate reports for an entire class.
Reports can be downloaded and printed.
School leaders can view academic performance summaries.
Different schools' information remains completely separated.
The application works on computers, tablets and smartphones.
We should test with sample data first and then conduct a supervised pilot in a real school.

